Finding: {"title":"Webhook idempotency-insert fallback path is a non-atomic check-then-insert race","severity":"LOW","area":"Stripe webhook — idempotency","files":["src/app/api/stripe-webhook/route.ts"],"detail":"insertStripeWebhookReceipt() (lines 170-207) branches on `typeof insertBuilder.onConflictDoNothing === 'function'`. The real production driver (NeonDatabase from drizzle-orm/neon-serverless, confirmed via src/lib/db.ts) always exposes onConflictDoNothing, so the atomic upsert-guard path is always taken in production. The fallback branch (find-then-insert, no transaction, no reliance on the unique constraint) only executes against a test/mock db lacking that method, and is a genuine TOCTOU race if two webhook redeliveries land concurrently against that mock.","impact":"No production impact — the fallback is unreachable there. Only matters if a future refactor swaps the db client to something lacking onConflictDoNothing, or the mock is reused as a stand-in for a real environment.","recommendation":"Delete the dead fallback branch (fail loudly if onConflictDoNothing is missing) or add a comment stating explicitly it is test-only and unsafe for concurrent production use, since the unique index stripe_webhook_events_owner_provider_event_uniq is what actually guarantees idempotency in production.","confidence":"medium"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

